,"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.79,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Use the authenticated GitHub metadata API under repository administration rights for F20, then verify exact readback through the same principal.'","Endpoint granularity: the unit is a specific endpoint SURFACE, not the vendor; the plan does not name the exact update surface (e.g. gh repo edit --description / PATCH /repos/{owner}/{repo}) nor the readback surface.","GitHub separates the repository description/homepage (repo metadata) from repository topics (a distinct endpoint), so 'leaves topics unchanged' and 'leaves the homepage unchanged' are surface-dependent claims.","Evidence class: Partially-verified — the vendor and the description-edit operation are clearly achievable under admin auth, but the plan text leaves the exact surface unconfirmed. Auth precondition IS stated ('authenticated', 'repository administration rights', 'same principal')."],"finding":"The F20 GitHub integration is named only at the API-family level ('the authenticated GitHub metadata API') without identifying the specific endpoint or CLI subcommand used to edit the About description, and without a verification against --help/docs. The About 'description' surface is distinct from the topics surface (a separate GitHub endpoint) and homepage field; the plan's assertions that topics and homepage remain unchanged depend on exactly which surface the update touches, which the plan text does not pin down.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f11f3c9d2b3b5345b","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section, bullet: 'Use the authenticated GitHub metadata API under repository administration rights for F20, then verify exact readback through the same principal.'","norm_id":"nc93bbad560ebee49","priority":0.11,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer picks a write path that also mutates topics or homepage (or uses a broader settings call), silently violating t